course: dictionary
lesson: 6963
title: One word, many meanings: palm
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «A teenager in Wales cut a bagel while holding it in her palm.» Here palm means the inside of your hand, between your wrist and your fingers.
explain: «He rubs against the palm tree until his skin is pushed into great folds.» Here palm means a tall tree with no branches and a bunch of big leaves at the top. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the other words in the sentence?
explain: Palm can also be a verb. To palm a coin is to hide it in your hand, as a magician does. To palm something off is to get rid of something unwanted by giving it to someone else.
fact: Palm means the inside of your hand, between your wrist and your fingers.
fact: A palm tree is a tall tree with no branches and a bunch of big leaves at the top. It grows in warm places.
fact: «Know something like the palm of your hand» means you know it very well.
fact: In «Namaste», the greeting from India and Nepal, people press their palms together to show respect.
fact: To palm something off means to give something unwanted to someone else.
exercise: «A teenager in Wales cut a bagel while holding it in her palm.» In this sentence, what is a palm? | A tall tree with big leaves | A kind of bread | A hidden coin | *The inside of your hand
exercise: «Macaws ... its beak cracks palm nuts so hard people need a hammer.» What are palm nuts? | Bits of a bagel | Tiny leaves | *Nuts from a palm tree | Coins from a magician
exercise: A magician makes a coin vanish. What does palm mean here? | *To hide something in your hand | The inside of your hand | To give something unwanted away | A tall tree with big leaves
test: «He rubs against the palm tree until his skin is pushed into great folds.» What is a palm tree? | *A tall tree with no branches and big leaves at the top | The inside of your hand | A kind of bread | A coin hidden by a magician
test: What does it mean to know something like the palm of your hand? | *To know it very well | To know nothing about it | To hold it tightly | To have sweaty palms
exam: A child palms a sweet into a pocket when no one is looking. What does palm mean? | The inside of your hand | A tall tree with big leaves | To give away something unwanted | *To hide something in your hand
